             covered while an agent walked straight past it. Plus the audit
             rows, the Phase 9d metering integration, and the blob store's
             scope partitioning + concurrent-admission race. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\ComputeBudgetTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 7c — data-object orphan-blob sweep: a real Save severed
             between its content and metadata writes produces the orphan,
             then the grace window (deferred vs reclaimed, one stamp
             apart) and the reverse reference (live content back-dated 400
             days and still untouched) are each pinned by a case that goes
             red alone if that half is dropped. Plus the preflight
             validator's four arms and the GP 13 keystone asserted on the
             service collection. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\DataObjectOrphanSweepTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 515 — upload-boundary content scanning. Structural arm
             (always on) covers the seam, the KB upload-path ordering, the
             audit row on every verdict, the GP 11/13 no-scanner path and
             the fail-open/closed split; the ClamAV reply grammar + frame
             encoding are pure and pinned alongside. Live arm is gated on
             TOOLUP_CLAMAV_HOST — no daemon, no Docker in VerifyAll. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\ContentScannerTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 9m.B — RAG-specific config validators (extension).
             Each of the four gap-audit validators is pinned by a red
             case asserting on the REMEDY its message names, a green case
             so the red one is not vacuous, and a gating case proving it
             stays silent on deployments the concern does not apply to —
             including the cross-validator pin that the local-embedder
             pair never both fire on one deployment. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\RagConfigValidatorExtensionTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 320 — external-compute completion-callback ingress: the
             IExternalHandleStore contract bound over both implementations
             (including the atomic MarkTerminal under 32-way concurrency),
             the secret mint/verify pair, the language-neutral wire
             contract, the push-resolves-with-zero-polls assertion, the
             concurrent callback-vs-poll race with its OWN ungated control
             (an always-wins store must produce a double, else the gated
             test is not measuring the gate), and the GP 13 pins that a
             default deployment composes neither store nor sink. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\ExternalCallbackTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 322 — the generic HTTP/REST external-compute companion,
             bound against a REAL in-process compute service on a real
             socket (an HttpMessageHandler stub would verify the half that
             is not in doubt and elide header names reaching the wire, a
             404 arriving as a status code, and a budget expiring against a
             server that genuinely does not answer). Carries the Phase 324
             contract pack UNMODIFIED, the per-call credential read pinned
             by a mid-run rotation with its own control, the retry
             classification table (5xx / 408 / 429 / timeout retriable;
             other 4xx terminal), and push completion end to end — the
             service calls the real Phase 320 ingress back over a socket,
             with a forged-secret control beside it. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\HttpComputeDispatcherTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 486 — signed worker outcomes: the header envelope's
             parse/render round-trip and its refusal shapes, the
             IWorkerKeyRegistry laws bound over BOTH implementations
             (sticky revocation, key-substitution refusal, pending is not
             usable), the verifier with a positive CONTROL beside every
             refusal (the tampered-artifact test proves the same genuine
             envelope verifies over its own body), the policy asserted in
             BOTH directions at the HTTP boundary, and the GP 13 pin that a
             deployment composing no verification does not read the header
             at all. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\SignedWorkerOutcomeTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 321 — job progress checkpoints: the checkpoint type's
             clamping, the pure coalescing rule WITH mutation controls
             pinning that terminal/durable are evaluated before the
             interval window (reordering them turns those two cases red),
             the burst test asserting BOTH that intermediates were shed and
             that the terminal frame survived, the durable-vs-transient
             split in both directions, and the GP 13 pin that an
             unconfigured deployment generates zero notification and zero
             event traffic. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\JobProgressTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 638 — the federated model-execution profile: two
             instances in one process, with the fit executing data-side
             and every row-access name the profile enumerates refused as
             a row read (paired with a positive control on the same
             registration, so "everything was refused" cannot pass). The
             governed-diagnostics cases carry a probe asserting that an
             undeclared projection is refused BEFORE it runs, and the
             scope cases carry the control that an assertion AGREEING
             with the binding is not refused — so the refusal is about
             the disagreement and not about assertions existing. -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\FederatedModelExecutionTests.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 336 — fail-closed dispatch consistency: the surface gate's
             missing-Subject seam and the PlatformAdmin backstop's premium
             discriminator, both pinned closed alongside the correct-path
             behaviour they must not disturb (GP 11). -->
        <Compile Include="InProcess\FailClosedDispatchTests.fs" />
        <Compile Include="Program.fs" />
